WEBVTT

00:01:39.420 --> 00:01:43.330
Letting your mouth stay wide
open that way is unsightly.

00:01:49.660 --> 00:01:52.840
Do you guys know each other?

00:02:06.720 --> 00:02:09.820
Are you going to keep acting like
you know nothing about this?

00:02:09.820 --> 00:02:13.490
Well, it definitely is a Modern-Day
Magic Code...

00:02:13.490 --> 00:02:16.970
It really does look a lot like mine.

00:02:16.970 --> 00:02:18.740
See, look at you!

00:02:18.740 --> 00:02:22.330
You're the one who summoned those Daemons
in the first place, aren't you?

00:02:23.150 --> 00:02:26.820
Do you two know each other?

00:02:26.820 --> 00:02:28.860
We ran into each other
a long time ago.

00:02:28.860 --> 00:02:32.540
Regarding this, am I going against
you or along with you?

00:02:32.540 --> 00:02:37.190
Hey, I've never been against
you in the first place.

00:02:37.190 --> 00:02:38.720
Yeah, right.

00:02:40.060 --> 00:02:42.480
Nothing strange with
the device driver.

00:02:42.480 --> 00:02:44.700
Nothing strange with
the swap file.

00:02:44.700 --> 00:02:47.560
Nothing strange with the
deleted files, either.

00:02:48.350 --> 00:02:52.220
I don't really see anything in the free
space sectors of the hard drive...

00:02:52.220 --> 00:02:53.220
No, wait.

00:03:06.100 --> 00:03:07.770
This melody is...

00:03:08.830 --> 00:03:13.460
This is a worm that I developed.

00:03:14.040 --> 00:03:17.470
And someone or something introduced
a different Code into it.

00:03:17.470 --> 00:03:20.020
So, that means it wasn't you.

00:03:20.020 --> 00:03:22.010
I've been saying that all along.

00:03:22.650 --> 00:03:24.370
I'm sorry.

00:03:24.370 --> 00:03:27.510
Um, what happened, exactly?

00:03:27.510 --> 00:03:34.730
Basically, Yumiko jumped the gun and came
here thinking I was the one responsible,

00:03:34.730 --> 00:03:37.390
when, in fact, it was
a modified virus.

00:03:37.650 --> 00:03:41.310
Actually, weren't you the one who
made the virus in the first place?

00:03:41.310 --> 00:03:44.650
Can you even imagine how much
trouble that Daemon gave me?

00:03:44.650 --> 00:03:48.640
That's why I'm going to
help you, Yumiko.

00:03:49.100 --> 00:03:50.620
Help me?

00:03:50.620 --> 00:03:52.440
You, of all people?

00:03:53.170 --> 00:03:56.660
Yeah. This is pretty interesting,
don't you think?

00:03:59.950 --> 00:04:02.760
So, basically, the next day
we don't have school,

00:04:02.760 --> 00:04:06.800
we're going to try to find clues about the guy
responsible for modifying the Daemons.

00:04:07.170 --> 00:04:08.790
Really.

00:04:08.790 --> 00:04:12.350
We'll be going around gathering information
and interviewing people.

00:04:12.730 --> 00:04:15.290
You sure it's okay for
us to tag along?

00:04:15.290 --> 00:04:19.860
Yeah! They said they'd be really happy
to have more girls with them.

00:04:21.050 --> 00:04:22.600
Who did?

00:04:24.240 --> 00:04:25.980
It's hot.

00:04:25.980 --> 00:04:28.470
And when it's hot, you
go to a water park.

00:04:28.470 --> 00:04:30.790
And at water parks, you
wear swimsuits.

00:04:30.790 --> 00:04:34.440
And when it comes to swimsuits,
you've gotta have cute girls.

00:04:36.160 --> 00:04:37.650
All right!

00:04:37.650 --> 00:04:41.780
Swimming with cute girls who'll make
your heart melt everywhere you look!

00:04:41.780 --> 00:04:43.560
Let's do it!

00:04:43.560 --> 00:04:46.850
Huh? You're not making any sense.

00:04:46.850 --> 00:04:49.540
And besides, aren't you a bit old
to be calling yourself a gir-

00:04:49.540 --> 00:04:51.360
Oh, Yumiko.

00:04:52.980 --> 00:04:56.730
What's wrong? You're wearing
that heavy thing...

00:04:57.660 --> 00:05:00.510
And look at what you're wearing!

00:05:00.510 --> 00:05:03.320
Does this place really have anything
to do with the culprit?

00:05:03.810 --> 00:05:06.240
Of course not.

00:05:06.810 --> 00:05:09.360
You have plenty of free
time, don't you?

00:05:09.360 --> 00:05:12.730
Everyone, wait for me!

00:05:15.960 --> 00:05:16.870
My, my.

00:05:17.320 --> 00:05:19.360
O-Ow...

00:05:24.390 --> 00:05:25.920
Oh, my.

00:05:28.770 --> 00:05:31.020
Surge up, my Code!

00:05:31.320 --> 00:05:33.850
It might be better
for you to stop.

00:05:33.850 --> 00:05:35.020
Yumiko!

00:05:40.790 --> 00:05:43.020
That's why I was saying that...

00:05:48.180 --> 00:05:50.370
P-Pink...

00:05:55.760 --> 00:05:57.620
Wait there!

00:06:08.050 --> 00:06:10.260
Prepare yourself, Misa!

00:06:11.480 --> 00:06:13.880
I think you're misunderstanding
something again.

00:06:13.880 --> 00:06:15.390
I didn't do tha-

00:06:15.390 --> 00:06:18.510
Transform to swords, my Code!

00:06:18.990 --> 00:06:22.910
Listen to everything
I'm saying first!

00:06:24.400 --> 00:06:25.790
I won't let you get away!

00:06:26.250 --> 00:06:29.700
Isn't it dangerous to
use magic here?

00:06:30.050 --> 00:06:31.660
Rest assured,

00:06:31.660 --> 00:06:34.910
I won't screw up and let civilians
get hurt or anything like that.

00:06:35.380 --> 00:06:37.910
You're trying to hurt me!

00:06:37.910 --> 00:06:40.240
You're an exception.

00:06:40.240 --> 00:06:42.120
That's mean!

00:06:42.690 --> 00:06:47.550
Running by the poolside is dangerous!

00:06:45.330 --> 00:06:47.550
I think we should stop them.

00:06:48.480 --> 00:06:50.580
You're a coward for
constantly running!

00:06:52.180 --> 00:06:54.100
I'm tired.

00:06:54.550 --> 00:06:58.170
In that case, I'll end this.

00:06:58.170 --> 00:07:01.370
Transform to swords, my Code!

00:07:18.060 --> 00:07:19.870
You're just trying to
block my sight!

00:07:22.630 --> 00:07:24.450
Huh? Not there?

00:07:25.520 --> 00:07:26.690
Where is she?

00:07:26.690 --> 00:07:28.510
Over here.

00:07:30.060 --> 00:07:33.500
How much of a coward are you?

00:07:34.140 --> 00:07:35.650
There!

00:07:40.740 --> 00:07:43.470
You can't use any magic
like that, can you?

00:07:43.960 --> 00:07:45.930
That's not fair!

00:07:45.930 --> 00:07:49.370
Well, you don't listen to
what people are saying.

00:07:49.370 --> 00:07:50.950
That doesn't mean-

00:07:50.950 --> 00:07:53.310
Get off me, already.

00:07:53.880 --> 00:07:55.750
Wh-Where are you touching me?

00:07:55.750 --> 00:07:57.490
I'm sorry!

00:07:58.490 --> 00:08:00.480
O-Ow.

00:08:01.420 --> 00:08:02.540
Huh?

00:08:04.290 --> 00:08:07.100
I-I'm sorry...

00:08:09.260 --> 00:08:12.540
I-I'm sorry!

00:08:15.940 --> 00:08:18.790
Morishita, feel better.

00:08:19.660 --> 00:08:24.200
Let's go down the water slide,
so you'll feel better.

00:08:25.620 --> 00:08:27.410
I'll be going first.

00:08:27.410 --> 00:08:28.810
Kaho-chan!

00:08:29.810 --> 00:08:31.070
Kaho-chan...

00:08:31.070 --> 00:08:33.340
Miss, you're up.

00:08:33.340 --> 00:08:34.450
Okay!

00:09:03.940 --> 00:09:05.650
Morishita?

00:09:07.270 --> 00:09:09.710
I thought I was going to die.

00:09:09.710 --> 00:09:11.760
Can you not swim?

00:09:11.760 --> 00:09:16.330
N-No. I just can't float in water...

00:09:16.330 --> 00:09:19.870
I don't think you can call
that being able to swim.

00:09:30.210 --> 00:09:31.680
Feel better?

00:09:31.680 --> 00:09:35.000
Yeah! Thanks, Kaho-chan!

00:09:55.720 --> 00:09:58.190
I've been looking for you, Huang.

00:09:58.840 --> 00:10:00.460
Anehara-san.

00:10:00.460 --> 00:10:03.660
Looks like you're up to the
same old shady things.

00:10:05.660 --> 00:10:07.920
Is that all you have to say?

00:10:08.460 --> 00:10:10.970
You'll die a bad death soon.

00:10:10.970 --> 00:10:14.510
That's fine. I've already taken
that into account.

00:10:14.900 --> 00:10:17.570
Why are you dressed like that?

00:10:17.570 --> 00:10:19.720
It's nothing other than cosplay.

00:10:23.200 --> 00:10:25.570
I found a worm that interests me.

00:10:26.330 --> 00:10:30.000
I thought you might
know who made it.

00:10:33.000 --> 00:10:34.320
Where did you find this?

00:10:34.950 --> 00:10:37.080
That's a secret.

00:10:37.580 --> 00:10:40.710
Is that the attitude you should have
when asking for something?

00:10:41.220 --> 00:10:44.410
You and I are friends, aren't we?

00:10:44.410 --> 00:10:47.730
I don't quite remember
us making it that far.

00:10:49.780 --> 00:10:52.600
This is probably Jinzai
Tsukumo's work.

00:10:52.600 --> 00:10:54.650
Jinzai Tsukumo...

00:10:54.650 --> 00:10:58.150
I met him at an internet workshop for the
Information Processing Association.

00:10:58.720 --> 00:11:03.880
Until recently, he was part of a company
called Japan Network Systems.

00:11:03.880 --> 00:11:05.860
Was part of?

00:11:05.860 --> 00:11:07.350
Where is he now?

00:11:08.270 --> 00:11:10.180
He isn't anywhere.

00:11:11.300 --> 00:11:13.370
Jinzai is dead.

00:11:20.900 --> 00:11:23.160
You can't swim?

00:11:23.870 --> 00:11:28.630
I can too! I just can't breathe
properly sometimes!

00:11:28.630 --> 00:11:31.850
I don't think you can call
that being able to swim.

00:11:34.380 --> 00:11:35.240
Huh?

00:11:35.240 --> 00:11:36.230
Huh? Huh?

00:11:36.230 --> 00:11:38.170
Kaho-chan!

00:11:40.210 --> 00:11:43.160
I'm fine. I can get back
there by myself.

00:12:02.240 --> 00:12:05.190
Morishita, behind you.

00:12:05.190 --> 00:12:07.200
Watch out.

00:12:14.660 --> 00:12:17.580
Here's the information
you wanted.

00:12:18.680 --> 00:12:21.090
Seems like the guy's
dead, though.

00:12:21.390 --> 00:12:22.710
When did that happen?

00:12:24.910 --> 00:12:27.120
What do you plan on
doing with Koyomi?

00:12:28.800 --> 00:12:31.500
I'm talking about that
summoning magic.

00:12:32.470 --> 00:12:34.720
It really seems like
a joke, doesn't it?

00:12:35.230 --> 00:12:37.520
It's nothing to laugh about.

00:12:37.520 --> 00:12:41.240
Her way is fatal for a mage.

00:12:42.030 --> 00:12:45.500
I don't think she's suited for
it personality-wise either.

00:12:45.500 --> 00:12:47.950
Are you speaking from
experience?

00:12:48.460 --> 00:12:50.480
That has nothing to do with it!

00:12:50.960 --> 00:12:53.320
I understand what
you want to say,

00:12:53.320 --> 00:12:55.330
but ultimately, it's
Koyomi's choice.

00:12:55.770 --> 00:12:57.430
You just do as you like!

00:12:57.430 --> 00:12:59.400
Nothing has changed
since six years ago.

00:12:59.860 --> 00:13:03.000
I'm trying to be a good teacher,
despite how I seem.

00:13:04.240 --> 00:13:07.460
It's why I even brought
you along today.

00:13:08.740 --> 00:13:10.390
What do you mean?

00:13:10.390 --> 00:13:12.530
Hey, isn't she in trouble?

00:13:12.530 --> 00:13:13.630
Morishita!

00:13:22.440 --> 00:13:23.600
Who?

00:13:24.070 --> 00:13:25.460
Who is that?

00:13:37.110 --> 00:13:38.480
Morishita!

00:13:38.480 --> 00:13:39.960
I'm going to call for help.

00:13:39.960 --> 00:13:41.400
Give her CPR!

00:13:41.400 --> 00:13:43.530
Huh, m-me?

00:13:44.210 --> 00:13:46.040
I will do it!

00:13:54.000 --> 00:13:57.190
I'm glad you were okay.

00:13:57.190 --> 00:13:59.480
Morishita... I'm glad.

00:14:00.430 --> 00:14:03.920
Why am I here?

00:14:03.920 --> 00:14:07.780
You were drowning, and
Ichinose saved you.

00:14:08.930 --> 00:14:10.520
Jeez...

00:14:10.960 --> 00:14:14.370
Just how much trouble
do you plan to give us?

00:14:15.830 --> 00:14:17.590
Thanks...

00:14:20.720 --> 00:14:22.190
Koyomi!

00:14:29.840 --> 00:14:31.310
Did you wake up?

00:14:32.790 --> 00:14:35.110
Uh, where am I?

00:14:35.600 --> 00:14:39.670
Drowning and then passing out...
You're a busy girl, aren't you?

00:14:39.670 --> 00:14:40.890
Drowning...

00:14:40.890 --> 00:14:42.800
Don't push yourself too hard.

00:14:44.330 --> 00:14:46.900
Um, what song were you
singing just now?

00:14:47.310 --> 00:14:51.290
My mom used to sing it a lot
while she was cooking.

00:14:51.290 --> 00:14:53.890
Your mom?

00:14:54.200 --> 00:14:56.510
She was really good at cooking,

00:14:56.510 --> 00:14:59.230
and on top of that, she was a genius
when it came to magic.

00:14:59.230 --> 00:15:02.230
She died right after giving
birth to Soshiro, though.

00:15:02.620 --> 00:15:03.920
I'm sorry.

00:15:04.250 --> 00:15:05.370
It's fine.

00:15:06.590 --> 00:15:10.040
Actually, it's my fault...

00:15:13.260 --> 00:15:15.570
How long are you going
to keep doing that?

00:15:15.570 --> 00:15:18.170
Shut up for a second.

00:15:19.080 --> 00:15:21.510
Are you okay now, Morishita?

00:15:21.510 --> 00:15:24.770
Yeah! I'm sorry for
making you worry.

00:15:25.380 --> 00:15:28.410
Yumiko-chan, thanks for before.

00:15:28.410 --> 00:15:30.690
No need to thank me.

00:15:30.690 --> 00:15:32.150
Did you find it?

00:15:33.270 --> 00:15:36.700
Yes. I do feel a Code.

00:15:37.070 --> 00:15:39.570
It's a Daemon, isn't it?

00:15:40.970 --> 00:15:44.710
Doesn't look like we can let
it continue on its rampage.

00:15:45.020 --> 00:15:49.290
Again? All that happened was the
small girl nearly drowning.

00:15:49.290 --> 00:15:53.840
I guess we have no choice but to tear
through everything in the park.

00:15:54.670 --> 00:15:56.610
Let's split up and search.

00:16:13.270 --> 00:16:15.480
Oh, Yumiko-chan.

00:16:15.480 --> 00:16:16.550
Find anything?

00:16:16.550 --> 00:16:19.430
No, what about you?

00:16:19.430 --> 00:16:21.120
Nothing here, either.

00:16:21.120 --> 00:16:23.000
That's weird.

00:16:23.610 --> 00:16:25.870
I'm sure I felt a Code.

00:16:26.810 --> 00:16:31.170
Um... I wonder if all
Daemons are bad.

00:16:31.490 --> 00:16:33.220
What do you mean?

00:16:33.220 --> 00:16:36.400
I can't really explain it well,

00:16:36.400 --> 00:16:39.150
but it was spinning
and jumping out!

00:16:39.150 --> 00:16:41.510
It looked like it was having fun!

00:16:42.020 --> 00:16:47.330
I've never heard of Daemons communicating
with humans.

00:16:47.330 --> 00:16:49.820
B-But I really did hear something!

00:16:50.580 --> 00:16:52.820
Something's weird.

00:16:53.830 --> 00:16:56.070
The waves are retreating.

00:16:56.470 --> 00:16:57.990
What's going on?

00:16:57.990 --> 00:17:00.160
It's probably just broken.

00:17:00.660 --> 00:17:02.570
I've heard of this.

00:17:03.020 --> 00:17:05.320
Right before a large wave comes,

00:17:05.320 --> 00:17:08.320
the water in the ocean
recedes like this.

00:17:08.760 --> 00:17:10.060
Hm...

00:17:16.000 --> 00:17:17.230
Yumiko-chan!

00:17:17.750 --> 00:17:19.250
Stay there!

00:17:20.630 --> 00:17:23.180
You'll just get in the way
if you follow me!

00:17:30.350 --> 00:17:33.570
With my strength,
can I hold it off?

00:17:38.060 --> 00:17:40.590
Your stride, itself, becomes time.

00:17:40.590 --> 00:17:42.610
I turn my back on you
and walk away.

00:17:46.070 --> 00:17:50.130
No matter how fleet Achilles,
or how quick the bullet,

00:17:51.370 --> 00:17:52.980
you will wander forever.

00:17:52.980 --> 00:17:57.030
Wander the endless corridor.

00:17:57.030 --> 00:17:58.890
Wander forever.

00:17:59.780 --> 00:18:03.130
Become the shield that blocks
the lance, my Code!

00:18:07.340 --> 00:18:08.640
Wow!

00:18:08.640 --> 00:18:10.390
But she's getting pushed back.

00:18:11.830 --> 00:18:13.510
At this rate...

00:18:13.510 --> 00:18:15.900
Not yet. Last a bit longer.

00:18:15.900 --> 00:18:18.840
Misa! Where have you
been all this time?

00:18:18.840 --> 00:18:21.950
You should think a bit more of
your actions' consequences.

00:18:21.950 --> 00:18:23.900
I don't need your advice!

00:18:23.900 --> 00:18:26.710
See? You're getting pushed back.

00:18:27.760 --> 00:18:29.880
And what exactly
are you planning?

00:18:29.880 --> 00:18:32.380
Basically, all we need is
to change the energy

00:18:32.380 --> 00:18:34.630
of the wave's momentum
into something else.

00:18:34.630 --> 00:18:36.030
There we go. All done.

00:18:36.400 --> 00:18:37.390
Take this!

00:18:47.780 --> 00:18:49.500
What is this?

00:18:49.500 --> 00:18:52.000
I magically raised the
water's viscosity.

00:18:52.500 --> 00:18:55.080
I didn't know there was
any magic like this.

00:18:57.670 --> 00:18:58.740
Wait a second!

00:19:02.620 --> 00:19:03.720
Yumiko-chan!

00:19:03.720 --> 00:19:05.240
Misa-san!

00:19:06.950 --> 00:19:11.310
Yes, we're fine.

00:19:15.660 --> 00:19:17.820
It's all sticky.

00:19:20.080 --> 00:19:21.870
I heard...

00:19:22.180 --> 00:19:24.270
I heard it again.

00:19:24.270 --> 00:19:30.040
I knew Koyomi could
hear her voice.

00:19:36.110 --> 00:19:39.900
Become the key which lights
the way, my Code.

00:19:41.800 --> 00:19:43.180
What is this?

00:19:43.180 --> 00:19:45.710
Looks like the facility that
circulates the water.

00:19:45.710 --> 00:19:50.020
I wonder if all the water in
the park is regulated here.

00:19:54.950 --> 00:19:57.710
This is it, isn't it?

00:20:00.420 --> 00:20:02.320
Wh-What?

00:20:06.160 --> 00:20:08.590
Morishita, is something there?

00:20:09.600 --> 00:20:11.560
But she's right there.

00:20:12.790 --> 00:20:14.490
That's a jini.

00:20:14.970 --> 00:20:17.510
I guess it's like a spirit that
lives through objects.

00:20:17.510 --> 00:20:23.320
It's rather unstable. I guess
it's out of control.

00:20:23.320 --> 00:20:25.640
So, that was the accident's
source.

00:20:26.860 --> 00:20:30.660
This is the voice that
I've been hearing!

00:20:31.010 --> 00:20:32.360
I see.

00:20:32.360 --> 00:20:38.520
I'm sure, in her own way, she was trying to
entertain you and the park's other guests.

00:20:38.520 --> 00:20:40.180
In any event,

00:20:40.180 --> 00:20:41.960
if she's going to cause
humans harm,

00:20:41.960 --> 00:20:44.020
then we have no choice
but to eliminate her.

00:20:44.020 --> 00:20:46.130
W-Wait!

00:20:46.640 --> 00:20:47.940
Move out of the way.

00:20:48.500 --> 00:20:51.420
B-But, I feel bad for her!

00:20:51.860 --> 00:20:55.450
Stop opening your mouth before
having any logical thought.

00:20:56.090 --> 00:20:57.430
Yumiko.

00:20:58.410 --> 00:21:00.500
I understand how Koyomi feels.

00:21:00.910 --> 00:21:02.440
But if she's left to
her own devices,

00:21:02.440 --> 00:21:04.030
another accident like
before will take place.

00:21:05.260 --> 00:21:07.880
You can't fix her?

00:21:08.270 --> 00:21:09.520
No.

00:21:10.200 --> 00:21:12.640
Once a program has
begun executing,

00:21:12.640 --> 00:21:14.620
you can't rewrite it in that phase.

00:21:14.620 --> 00:21:15.390
But!

00:21:15.390 --> 00:21:16.690
Morishita.

00:21:21.910 --> 00:21:24.710
Your role is over.

00:21:25.120 --> 00:21:27.400
Sleep.

00:21:49.700 --> 00:21:53.030
Koyomi, I'll tell it to you straight.

00:21:53.510 --> 00:21:55.910
You should stop dealing
with magic.

00:21:58.040 --> 00:22:01.880
You're not suited
to being a mage.

00:23:46.270 --> 00:23:48.590
A mage will go after
a silver-haired girl,

00:23:48.590 --> 00:23:51.560
to try to reach the Sorceress's
Library.

00:23:52.220 --> 00:23:55.920
Six years ago on December 24th,

00:23:55.920 --> 00:23:58.590
that's when it will all begin.

00:24:04.560 --> 00:24:07.040
About jini

00:24:07.840 --> 00:24:10.710
Hi! Morishita Koyomi here!

00:24:10.710 --> 00:24:13.960
Let's have a fun time
studying together!

00:24:13.960 --> 00:24:17.030
Hello there. Anehara Misa here.

00:24:17.030 --> 00:24:20.460
This time, we'll be learning
about the jini.

00:24:20.460 --> 00:24:22.660
Teacher!

00:24:22.660 --> 00:24:27.480
jini are the fairy-like things that
appeared this episode, right?

00:24:27.480 --> 00:24:29.120
That's right.

00:24:29.120 --> 00:24:35.160
jini are like spirits that live through
items like electronics.

00:24:35.160 --> 00:24:38.050
So, Daemons are different?

00:24:38.050 --> 00:24:41.510
Daemons are summoned
from a parallel world,

00:24:41.510 --> 00:24:46.440
whereas jini don't actually exist,
but they come from objects-

00:24:46.440 --> 00:24:50.760
Hm, for example, a cell phone has certain
functions it performs, right?

00:24:50.760 --> 00:24:53.850
So basically, it'd be like
a virtual personality

00:24:53.850 --> 00:24:55.690
bestowed upon those functions
through magic.

00:24:55.690 --> 00:24:57.830
They're the same
in the sense that

00:24:57.830 --> 00:25:00.260
neither actually exists
in this world,

00:25:00.260 --> 00:25:01.530
but we can see them
because of magic.

00:25:01.530 --> 00:25:04.120
I see. That make sense.

00:25:04.120 --> 00:25:07.540
So, a-are they bad?

00:25:07.540 --> 00:25:11.230
The one that appeared in this episode
might have liked pranks,

00:25:11.230 --> 00:25:14.660
but jini and Daemons aren't
particularly bad.

00:25:14.660 --> 00:25:17.910
It might depend on who
they interact with.

00:25:17.910 --> 00:25:21.020
Who they interact with?

00:25:21.020 --> 00:25:23.770
Yes, a specific Daemon or jini

00:25:23.770 --> 00:25:27.520
might be good or bad, depending
on a person's point of view,

00:25:27.520 --> 00:25:30.760
but they don't have any sense
of good or evil themselves.

00:25:30.760 --> 00:25:33.400
Hm, I see.

00:25:33.400 --> 00:25:37.540
So, jini and Daemons behave differently, depending
on who they come in contact with.

00:25:37.540 --> 00:25:39.660
That's right.

00:25:39.660 --> 00:25:43.760
Good or evil, depending on
their remote control!

00:25:44.980 --> 00:25:47.140
What is that?

00:25:47.140 --> 00:25:51.070
If you don't know,
then that's fine.

00:25:51.070 --> 00:25:55.000
Don't say things like Kaho-chan
would say!

00:25:55.520 --> 00:26:00.790
There might be a jini in
your computer or TV.

00:26:00.790 --> 00:26:03.870
In any event, see you next week.

00:26:03.870 --> 00:26:07.420
Bye-bye!
